From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] qcacld: drop -Werror from the vendor Kbuild

This tree is built by LineageOS with the Android prebuilt clang, which does
not diagnose what GCC 15 does. Building qcacld-3.0 with OpenEmbedded's
aarch64 cross toolchain turns a pre-existing warning into a hard error and
the build stops in drivers/staging before it reaches vmlinux:

  wlan_hdd_cfg80211.c:1019:5: error: conflicting types for
  'wlan_hdd_send_hang_reason_event' due to enum/integer mismatch; have
  'int(struct hdd_context *, enum qdf_hang_reason, void *, size_t)'
  [-Werror=enum-int-mismatch]

That is a declaration in wlan_hdd_cfg80211.h using int where the definition
uses the enum - benign in practice on this ABI, and not something to fix
blind in a driver nobody here can test. -Wenum-int-mismatch is a GCC 13
diagnostic; the toolchain this code was written for had no opinion about it.

Only the unconditional -Werror is removed, and only in vendor code. The
-Werror=<specific> forms the top-level kernel Makefile sets are left alone,
and the warnings themselves are unchanged and still printed.

Unlike surya's equivalent patch this touches exactly one file: fajita's 4.9
tree keeps its audio drivers in sound/soc/msm rather than a techpack/ with
its own Kbuilds, and nothing under techpack/ here sets -Werror at all.

Same treatment as the surya (SM7150) and mindphone (MT6739) ports.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor tree is built with Android's clang]
---
 drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/Kbuild | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/Kbuild b/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/Kbuild
--- a/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/Kbuild
+++ b/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/Kbuild
@@ -1658,7 +1658,6 @@ ccflags-y += $(INCS)
 
 cppflags-y +=	-DANI_OS_TYPE_ANDROID=6 \
 		-Wall\
-		-Werror\
 		-D__linux__
 
 cppflags-$(CONFIG_PTT_SOCK_SVC_ENABLE) += -DPTT_SOCK_SVC_ENABLE
